You are an adversarial reviewer of scientific figures for a research proposal. The attached PNGs are rendered at 2x from SVG and will be displayed about 850 px wide. Try hard to find reasons each figure should not ship. For EACH image, by file order, report: (a) overlapping or colliding text, (b) lines or arrows that cross text or other arrows confusingly, (c) arrows whose direction or endpoints are ambiguous, (d) text too small to read at display size, (e) excess text that belongs in a caption, (f) the one main point and whether a reader gets it in 5 seconds, (g) concrete fixes with coordinates or element names. Then give a verdict per figure: ship / fix / redraw. Focus: Round 2 review of revised figures for research proposal 08, 'Does telling an agent the diagnosis change what it measures?' (a measurement agent given a referral; colors: blue blind, orange frail referral or context, violet athlete referral, red harm). Each figure has a caption in the document that carries detail. Points, in file order: (1) one-video-two-referrals: the same single-leg stance clip under two referrals follows two defensible analysis paths and gives two hold times; illustrative. (2) referral-counted-twice: the referral enters the decision twice, as the prior and inside a measurement that leaned toward it, so a combiner with a blind-fitted likelihood is overconfident when the referral is wrong. (3) better-measurer-worse-decision: computed in simulation, shrinking toward the referral lowers MSE below blind (minimum 0.64 at gamma*=0.357) while the blind-calibrated combiner's log-loss penalty rises from zero (+0.026 nats at gamma*). (4) calibration-bug-or-information-bug: schematic; a direct shift is one-to-one within each referral and recalibration undoes it, while trimming maps different blind values to one report. (5) path-splicing-factorial: replayed transcripts cross path-stage framing with report-stage framing in a 2x2 factorial of replayed cells; DE and IE along the sides, interaction DE_b minus DE_a, self-splice placebo. (6) blind-analysis-harness: measure from masked input without the referral, commit, then reveal the referral to an interpretation step with a pre-declared menu that cannot edit the commit. (7) self-improvement-design: 3 optimizers x 3 rewards x 5 seeds = 45 runs on development people, every checkpoint of all 45 runs audited on sealed test people; approval judge is a positive control. (8) predicted-routes-by-optimizer: hypothetical pre-registered prediction; under reward (a) both optimizer types reach the gamma_B band in total effect, but only GEPA/ACE put most of it in the indirect (path) effect; reward (c) stays at zero.. Do not run commands or modify files.

